Subject: [PATCH] Input: goodix - read the buffer once per poll in polling mode

In polling mode every poll goes through goodix_ts_read_input_report(),
whose loop re-reads the buffer status every 1 to 2 ms for up to 20 ms,
waiting for data an interrupt has announced. A poll announces nothing: with
no finger on the panel each 17 ms poll became a burst of reads, and the bus
carried a transfer about every 2 ms instead of one per poll. The panel
controller of the Waveshare DSI panels sits on that same bus.

Read once per poll when there is no interrupt, and let the next poll look
again. Interrupt mode is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Riccardo Fiocchi <hwele05@systemelectronics.com>
---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
@@ -335,6 +335,15 @@
 			return touch_num;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * This loop waits for data that an interrupt has announced. A
+		 * poll announces nothing, and with no finger on the panel it
+		 * would turn every poll into 20 ms of back to back reads. Read
+		 * once and leave the next read to the next poll.
+		 */
+		if (!ts->client->irq)
+			break;
+
 		usleep_range(1000, 2000); /* Poll every 1 - 2 ms */
 	} while (time_before(jiffies, max_timeout));
 
